Hi,

On Monday 05 November 2012, Rebel Tyrcus wrote:
> At work (windows) I was guesing is just a proxy problem. I remembered
> that for R I had to modifiy the direct access to the program in the
> desktop, starting R with the flag --internet2. Apparently, this causes
> R using IE proxy internals, otherwise R cannot connect to CRAN servers
> 
> "C:\Archivos de programa\R\R-2.15.2\bin\i386\Rgui.exe" --internet2
> 
> I guess that the same problem must apply in RKWard.

yes, if you have to do that in R, then most likely it is the same problem in 
RKWard, indeed. Since you won't be able to pass custom command line parameters 
to R, use
   setInternet2 (TRUE)
in the R Console window, after starting, and before accessing the net. If that 
fixes the problem, you can add this to Settings->Configure RKWard->R backend-
>Further commands to run in each session, in order to make it permanent.

Regards
Thomas
